{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["And the reason for <b>מֵאֶרֶץ הָעִבְרִים</b> (from the land of the Hebrews): it is the land of Hebron, where Abraham, Isaac, and Jacob dwelled. For Abraham, who was the head of the lineage, was called 'Abraham the Hebrew' (Genesis 14:13), because he came from across the river and his name was great among the nations, since 'and I will make your name great' (Genesis 12:2) was fulfilled in him. Therefore all his descendants were called Hebrews, and they themselves held fast to this name, so that they would not intermingle with the peoples of the Canaanite lands. And this name was established upon all the seed of Israel forever. And this is the reason for 'he brought us a Hebrew man' (Genesis 39:14): for Joseph told them 'I am a Hebrew,' and he did not want them to consider him a Canaanite. And he called the land of their sojournings 'the land of the Hebrews,' that is to say, the land where the Hebrews are. Or the land was so named because they were the great ones of the land and its nobles, as it is said (Genesis 23:6), 'you are a prince of Elohim among us,' and as it is written (Psalms 105:15), 'do not touch My anointed ones.'"], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 40, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:42:23.973795572Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}